// GENERATED by scripts/build-courses.ts from src/lib/courses/content — edit those files, then run: npm run courses
import type { LessonText } from '../types';
const text: LessonText[][] = [[{"say":"Bienvenue en Français 2! Let's review the irregular verbs you'll use every day.","blocks":[{"t":"key","text":"Key irregular verbs:"},{"t":"list","items":["faire (to do, make): je fais, tu fais, il fait, nous faisons, vous faites, ils font.","prendre (to take): je prends, nous prenons, ils prennent.","pouvoir (can): je peux, nous pouvons, ils peuvent.","vouloir (to want): je veux, nous voulons, ils veulent.","devoir (must): je dois, nous devons, ils doivent.","venir (to come): je viens, nous venons, ils viennent."]},{"t":"p","text":"Faire is used in many expressions: faire du sport, faire les devoirs (do homework), Il fait beau (the weather is nice)."},{"t":"p","text":"Modal verbs (pouvoir, vouloir, devoir) are followed by an infinitive: Je dois étudier."}]},{"say":"Reflexive verbs describe what you do to yourself. They're perfect for talking about your routine.","blocks":[{"t":"key","text":"Reflexive verbs use pronouns that match the subject: me, te, se, nous, vous, se. Se lever: je me lève, tu te lèves, il se lève, nous nous levons, vous vous levez, ils se lèvent."},{"t":"p","text":"Routine verbs: se réveiller (to wake up), se lever (to get up), se doucher (to shower), s'habiller (to get dressed), se brosser les dents (to brush one's teeth), se coucher (to go to bed)."},{"t":"p","text":"Negative: Je ne me lève pas tôt. The pronoun stays right before the verb."},{"t":"ex","problem":"Say \"I wake up at 7 and I get dressed.\"","steps":["se réveiller: je me réveille; s'habiller: je m'habille"],"answer":"Je me réveille à sept heures et je m'habille."}]}],[{"say":"The passé composé talks about completed past actions. It's the most common past tense in spoken French.","blocks":[{"t":"key","text":"Form: present tense of avoir + past participle. J'ai mangé (I ate / I have eaten)."},{"t":"p","text":"Regular past participles: -er → -é (parlé), -ir → -i (fini), -re → -u (vendu)."},{"t":"p","text":"Common irregular participles: avoir → eu, être → été, faire → fait, prendre → pris, voir → vu, lire → lu, boire → bu, écrire → écrit, mettre → mis."},{"t":"p","text":"Negative: ne…pas wraps around avoir: Je n'ai pas fini."},{"t":"ex","problem":"Say \"We watched a movie yesterday.\"","steps":["regarder → regardé; nous + avons"],"answer":"Hier, nous avons regardé un film."}]},{"say":"About 17 verbs, mostly verbs of motion, use être instead of avoir. And their participles agree!","blocks":[{"t":"key","text":"DR MRS VANDERTRAMP verbs use être: devenir, revenir, monter, rester, sortir, venir, aller, naître, descendre, entrer, retourner, tomber, rentrer, arriver, mourir, partir. All reflexive verbs also use être."},{"t":"p","text":"With être, the past participle agrees with the subject in gender and number: Elle est allée (add -e). Ils sont partis (add -s). Elles sont arrivées."},{"t":"ex","problem":"Say \"My sisters arrived late.\"","steps":["arriver uses être; subject is feminine plural"],"answer":"Mes sœurs sont arrivées en retard."},{"t":"oops","text":"Don't forget agreement with être verbs; it's one of the most common errors."}]}],[{"say":"The imparfait describes how things were and what used to happen. It sets the scene for stories.","blocks":[{"t":"key","text":"Form: take the nous present form, drop -ons, and add -ais, -ais, -ait, -ions, -iez, -aient. Nous parlons → je parlais. The only irregular stem is être: j'étais."},{"t":"p","text":"Uses: habits in the past (Quand j'étais petit, je jouais au foot), descriptions (Il faisait beau), feelings and states (J'avais peur), and ongoing actions."},{"t":"p","text":"Clue words: souvent (often), toujours (always), d'habitude (usually), autrefois (in the past), tous les jours (every day)."},{"t":"ex","problem":"Say \"When I was young, I lived in Lyon.\"","steps":["être → étais; habiter → habitais"],"answer":"Quand j'étais jeune, j'habitais à Lyon."}]},{"say":"Telling a story in French means mixing both past tenses. Here's how to choose.","blocks":[{"t":"key","text":"Passé composé: specific completed actions, events that move the story forward, and interruptions. Imparfait: background, descriptions, habits and ongoing actions."},{"t":"p","text":"Common pattern: an ongoing action (imparfait) is interrupted by an event (passé composé): Je dormais quand le téléphone a sonné."},{"t":"p","text":"Think of it as a play: the imparfait describes the stage and the scene; the passé composé is the action."},{"t":"ex","problem":"Choose: \"Il ___ (pleuvoir) quand nous ___ (sortir).\"","steps":["Rain is background: pleuvait","Going out is a completed event: sommes sortis"],"answer":"Il pleuvait quand nous sommes sortis."}]}],[{"say":"Pronouns help you avoid repeating nouns. French object pronouns go before the verb.","blocks":[{"t":"key","text":"Direct object pronouns replace the thing receiving the action: le, la, l', les. Je vois le film → Je le vois."},{"t":"p","text":"Indirect object pronouns replace à + person: lui (to him/her), leur (to them). Je parle à Marie → Je lui parle."},{"t":"p","text":"Me, te, nous, vous can be direct or indirect."},{"t":"p","text":"Y replaces à + place or thing (J'y vais = I'm going there). En replaces de + noun or quantities (J'en veux = I want some)."},{"t":"p","text":"Pronouns go before the conjugated verb (Je ne le vois pas) or before the infinitive (Je vais le voir)."}]},{"say":"Let's talk about what will happen and what would happen. Both tenses share the same stems.","blocks":[{"t":"key","text":"Future (futur simple): infinitive + -ai, -as, -a, -ons, -ez, -ont. Je parlerai (I will speak). For -re verbs, drop the final e: je vendrai."},{"t":"p","text":"Conditional: the same stem + imparfait endings: -ais, -ais, -ait, -ions, -iez, -aient. Je parlerais (I would speak)."},{"t":"p","text":"Irregular stems: être → ser-, avoir → aur-, aller → ir-, faire → fer-, pouvoir → pourr-, vouloir → voudr-, venir → viendr-, voir → verr-, devoir → devr-."},{"t":"p","text":"Si clauses: Si + present, future (Si j'ai le temps, je viendrai). Si + imparfait, conditional (Si j'avais de l'argent, je voyagerais)."}]}]];
export default text;
